## Spec review decision

The orchestrator asked whether the light lane needs a spec review. From the documents:

- The framework exempts only the final acceptance for the light lane (SKILL.md closeout standard and
  the closeout check, through metadata lane light). It has no light-lane exemption for the spec review.
- The spec header and the test-strategy header say light lane. test-strategy.md section 4 and the plan
  gate table drop Phase acceptance and Adversarial testing. Neither names the spec review.
- The track holds spec-review.md with a Round 1 by the build session: 2 Major and 2 Nit findings, all
  fixed. Its route is not recorded, and the spec author was opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash.

Decision: the spec review is needed in principle, and the build session met it in substance. The
orchestrator role spawn and its result file do not exist. I record a deviation (finding F2). No new
review is needed now, because Review A, the phase acceptance, and this role read the spec against the
finished code. The closeout check does not require a spec-review result. Independence from the spec
author cannot be checked, because the Round 1 route is not recorded.

